{
  "about": "Qt's own examples (the qtdoc submodule): where each starts, the window Qt gives it, what it needs, and whether the plain `qml` tool can run it here. corpus/reference.mjs and examples/gallery read this.",
  "fields": {
    "dir": "the example's directory, in `root`",
    "entry": "the QML file it starts from, in `dir`",
    "root": "what the entry's root object is: an Item (shown in a QQuickView) or a Window; `rootType` is the type as written",
    "load": "how the example's main.cpp loads the entry",
    "window": "the size of its window, and where that comes from; `imposed` when the example declares none and this is ours",
    "importPaths": "QML import paths it needs, in `dir`",
    "modules": "the example's own QML modules: URI to directory, in `dir`",
    "imports": "every other module its QML files import",
    "cpp": "what it needs from C++ of its own",
    "volatile": "why its picture is not the same twice: time, animation, network",
    "qt": "`runnable`: the `qml` tool of the Qt installed here renders it, or `reason` why not. For the run: `style` or `controlsConf` (the Controls style its main.cpp or resources choose), `env` (environment its main.cpp sets), `module` (the URI its files import it by), `properties` (initial properties main.cpp sets), `offline`, `settle` (ms before the picture, default 1500)"
  },
  "root": "qtdoc/examples",
  "screen": {
    "width": 1920,
    "height": 1080
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "alarms",
      "dir": "tutorials/alarms",
      "entry": "Main.qml",
      "root": "Window",
      "rootType": "ApplicationWindow",
      "load": "QQmlApplicationEngine::loadFromModule(\"AlarmsModule\", \"Main\")",
      "window": {
        "width": 400,
        "height": 500,
        "from": "ApplicationWindow in Main.qml"
      },
      "importPaths": [],
      "modules": {
        "AlarmsModule": "."
      },
      "imports": [
        "QtQuick",
        "QtQuick.Controls",
        "QtQuick.Controls.Material",
        "QtQuick.Layouts",
        "QtQuick.Window"
      ],
      "cpp": [],
      "qt": {
        "runnable": true,
        "controlsConf": "qtquickcontrols2.conf"
      },
      "notes": "The Material style, dark, from qtquickcontrols2.conf. The dates in the list are fixed (2018), so the picture does not change."
    },
    {
